WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.868
-My next guest is one of the
biggest models on the planet,

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.872
and she just launched
a brand-new YouTube channel

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.407
that you can check out
starting today.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:11.845
Here's our pal Hailey Bieber.
Hailey! Oh!

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.513
-It is so good to see.
-Hi!

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.283
-You were on here last year,

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.752
probably exact right
before the lockdown,

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:20.853
I think,
was the last time we talked.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:23.055
-Mm-hmm.
-And you and Justin

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:26.025
have been married for two years,
two and a half years?

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.827
Which technically means
that you've spent

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:31.297
half of your marriage so far
in quarantine.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.633
-Yeah, and that's exactly --
that's exactly what it is.

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:36.469
-According to social media,
what I saw,

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.305
it looks like there's
a lot of gaming going on.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.407
-There's a lot
of gaming going on.

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.009
-What's your jam,
as far as games go,

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:46.378
and does it get competitive?

00:00:46.378 --> 00:00:49.582
-Justin's a very competitive
person just in general.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.350
I mean, I guess
I'm pretty competitive, too.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:54.086
But the biggest thing
that was going on in our house

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:58.023
was a lot of "UNO,"
a lot of "Bananagrams."

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:00.960
I would like to say I think
that I'm the "UNO" champion,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.529
but that's like self-proclaimed,
so whatever.

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.966
-Wow!
-But, yeah, lots of "UNO."

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.001
-I love "UNO," too.
-Lots of "Bananagrams."

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:10.102
I love that game.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.537
I don't know if you know
what that is.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.772
-Is that where
you put the titles

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.675
and you spell the words,
and it's a race almost?

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.543
-Yeah.
-Yeah. I love that game.

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:18.944
I love "Bananagrams."
-Same.

00:01:18.944 --> 00:01:20.213
It's my absolute favorite.
-And it's in a little zipper,

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.281
in a banana, and like
a little zipper thing?

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:25.117
-Uh-huh. They also have one,
too, called "Word-A-Melon"

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.353
that's really fun.
-Oh, I don't know that one.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.956
-From the same people.
-Really?

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.724
-Yeah. You got to get into
"Word-A-Melon."

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.560
-I would tot-- "Word-A-Melon."
That's the best name for it.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.763
Are you kidding me?
Oh, I love that.

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.198
-Yeah. It's so fun.

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:43.136
-I also heard that he was --
you guys were playing chess.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.471
-Yeah. So, Justin's
really good at chess,

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.874
and he has played chess
since he was a kid,

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.275
and he was trying to --

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.744
This is also pre
"Queen's Gambit," by the way.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:54.914
He was trying to teach me
how to play chess,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.283
and he would win every time.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.951
So far, I haven't gotten
to beat him yet,

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:02.054
because I was a new learner,
and I was just learning as I go.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:05.524
So I think, honestly, low-key,
I think he just liked it

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.727
because he knew he was going
to win every time.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.029
-He's like, "Let's do one more
practice thing,"

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.397
and he just loves winning.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.566
I follow you on Instagram
and all the socials,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.401
but you've been doing
a very cool thing.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.270
You've been handing
over your Instagram

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:21.474
and having like social activists
and organizations take it over.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.743
What made you decide to do that?
I think it's great.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:26.979
-My point behind it was,
I wanted to reach out

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:30.583
to different people,
and if they were interested,

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.885
then just hand
over the Instagram

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:35.421
and let them talk about whatever
they were passionate about.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.456
And I wanted it to be
an educational thing,

00:02:37.456 --> 00:02:39.558
not only for the people
who follow me,

00:02:39.558 --> 00:02:41.561
but I wanted to learn
along with them.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.630
And I have been so inspired
and learned so much

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.832
from these incredible people.
And it's something

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:48.734
that I'm going to
definitely continue doing.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.736
-I want to talk about
some other exciting news.

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:52.872
Today was a huge day for you,

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:56.775
because you officially launched
a YouTube channel.

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:58.043
I can't believe
that you did this.

00:02:58.043 --> 00:03:00.345
Is this because of
the docu thing that you did,

00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:01.947
the docuseries?

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.816
-I have to say,
when "Seasons" was coming out,

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.652
I was really nervous about it
because I felt like

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:11.490
I had never allowed anybody
into my world in that way.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.295
And I'm -- you know,
I'm very protective of my space

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:17.263
and protective of my family

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.798
and the people that I love
and I care about.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.434
So it was something
that was a little bit

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.569
on the more
uncomfortable side for me.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.771
And then, what ended up
happening for me with "Seasons"

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.107
is, after the whole thing
came out,

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.809
the feedback that I got
from people,

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:32.311
not only
just friends and family

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.714
but just random people
would come up to me and be like,

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:36.282
"Hey, I saw you on 'Seasons,'

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:39.618
and, you know, I was really --
I was really surprised,"

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.120
or, "I really enjoyed it,"

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.389
and, "It was so nice to hear
from you in that way."

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:46.993
So it actually gave me
a confidence

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:50.797
and put me more in a space
of feeling like I was ready

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:54.300
to open myself up
as Hailey more to people.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.337
And another part of why
I wanted to do this is,

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:59.906
they can't twist
what I'm trying to say,

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:01.340
you know, from YouTube.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.808
It's coming straight
from my mouth.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.944
And I think that's something
that I battled with a lot

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:08.113
is people trying to twist
my words or the media

00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:10.082
taking something that I've said

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:13.652
or creating their own narratives
where if I control it,

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:17.223
that means that nobody can try
to turn it into something else.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.591
You're hearing it
straight from me.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.226
I can clear up
whatever I want to,

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.094
and that gives me
a lot of freedom, in a way.

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:25.264
-What kind of videos
are you gonna be making?

00:04:25.264 --> 00:04:26.732
-We're gonna do a bunch
of different things.

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:31.670
We started a show on there
called "Who's in My Bathroom?"

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.339
which is very funny,

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:36.442
where I'm going to have
different guests come on,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.710
and we're going to sit down
and we're gonna chat,

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.146
and we're gonna do weird,
quirky things in the bathroom.

00:04:41.146 --> 00:04:44.450
So the first episode that aired
today is with Kendall Jenner,

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.251
who is one of my best friends.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:46.251 --> 00:04:49.555
-And we made macaroni and cheese
in the bathroom,

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:50.923
and we played
"Never Have I Ever"

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:54.593
and drank tequila.
-Come on.

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:56.996
I mean, come on, sold.
I'm in.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.897
I'm watching. I can't wait.

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:01.267
-It's very fun.
It's lighthearted.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:03.836
And we also --
we also are gonna do things

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.671
where we have conversations
with different people

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:07.173
about things
that I'm passionate about.

00:05:07.173 --> 00:05:10.609
So we have a conversation
with a psychiatrist

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:12.778
named Dr. Jessica Clemons

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.880
where we talk about social media
and mental health.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.150
So I wanted it to have a range
of different things

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.519
that just have to do with me

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.353
and that are important to me
and that are fun for me,

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:22.521
that are part of my life,

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.357
and just let people in
a little bit more.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.193
-I love it.
You brought us a clip

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.861
from one of the videos.

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:31.397
Here is Hailey Bieber
and Kendall Jenner

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:33.232
playing a round of
"Never Have I Ever."

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.733
Take a look.

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:36.703
-Hoo! Okay, next question.

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:42.241
-Cheers.
I can say...

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.176
-Oh, yeah, wait, no, no.
If we haven't --

00:05:44.176 --> 00:05:46.211
[ Laughter ]
-Breaking news?!

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:47.947
I'm all, "Cheers [bleep]"

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:52.818
♪♪

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:55.421
I'm sorry. Okay.
Let's take that again.

00:05:55.421 --> 00:05:57.990
-We need to --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.759
-We got confused.
We've never been pregnant.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:02.461
Nothing of that sort.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.197
-Hailey Bieber,
it's always good to see you.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.265
Check out her new
YouTube channel,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.368
